"""AQS-BLD-017 foundation design against the soil data (X-BLD-03, A-M-208). Mat (raft) under the whole plate at the CATCH_TANK floor,
the basement walls retain soil. Checks: (1) gross and net bearing (net = gross - excavated overburden) under service D + F + L against
the IBC 1806.2 presumptive clay value (AQS-SITE-002); (2) bearing under seismic overturning (AQS-BLD-014 moment), with the reservoirs
full; (3) uplift with groundwater at the driver depth and the plant empty, reservoirs drained; (4) raft depth for two-way shear at the
heaviest interior column (ACI 318-19 22.6.5.2) from AQS-BLD-016. Run after _frame_check.py."""
import json, math, os, sys
R = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))); os.chdir(R); sys.path.insert(0, R); sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(R, 'models/freecad'))
from flow_graph.param.refs import cite
from flow_graph.param import site as SITE   # apparent gravity from the site profile
from flow_graph.param import drivers as DR, water_tower as WT
for k in ('IBC2027_1806', 'ACI318_19', 'ASCE7_22'): cite(k)
import params as P
d = DR.load(); v = lambda k: DR.val(d, k); qa = v('soil_allow_kPa'); gs = v('soil_unit_weight_kN_m3'); gw = v('gw_depth_m'); fc = v('raft_fc_MPa')
Lp, Wp = P.PLATE_L/1000, P.PLATE_W/1000; A = Lp*Wp
FC = json.load(open('docs-authority/inventory/FRAME_CHECK.json')); Pu_int = FC['cols'][-1][2]['interior'][0]; b_col = FC['cols'][-1][2]['interior'][1]['b']/1000
SL = {}
for line in open('docs-authority/STRUCT_LOADS.md'):
    c = [x.strip() for x in line.split('|')]
    if len(c) > 8 and c[1][:1] in 'LR':
        try: SL[c[1]] = dict(empty=float(c[4]), op=float(c[5]))
        except ValueError: pass
r = P.HYDRO; depth = -r['z_catch_floor_m'] + P.SLAB_THK/1000                                                       # m below grade to the raft underside (approx. catch floor)
slab = P.SLAB_THK/1000*24.0; nlev = 8                                   # suspended levels L-1..ROOF
LIVE = {'L-1': 6.0, 'L0': 6.0, 'L1': 4.79, 'L2': 4.79, 'ROOF': 0.96}
frame_kN = sum(sum(x[2][c][1]['kg_m'] for c in x[2]) / 3 * x[1] for x in FC['cols']) * 20 * SITE.g()*1e-3   # column steel, 20 columns (average of the three types)
walls_kN = 2*(Lp + Wp)*depth*0.6*24.0                                  # 600 mm basement walls
def raft_t():
    for t in [x/100 for x in range(60, 400, 5)]:
        dd = t - 0.1; b0 = 4*(b_col + dd); phiVc = 0.75*0.33*math.sqrt(fc)*b0*dd*1000    # kN
        if phiVc >= Pu_int: return t, phiVc
t_raft, phiVc = raft_t(); raft_kN = A*t_raft*24.0
D_eq = sum(s['empty'] for s in SL.values()); OP = sum(s['op'] for s in SL.values())
W_srv = nlev*slab*A + frame_kN + walls_kN + raft_kN + OP + sum(LIVE.values())*A
W_empty = nlev*slab*A + frame_kN + walls_kN + raft_kN + D_eq
U = SITE.g()*max(0.0, depth - gw)*A; t_shear = t_raft
dt = max(0.0, (1.10*U - W_empty)/(A*(24.0 - 1.10*SITE.g())))               # thicken the raft downward until FS 1.10 (ballast from need)
dt = math.ceil(dt*20)/20; t_raft += dt; depth += dt; raft_kN += A*dt*24.0; W_empty += A*dt*24.0; W_srv += A*dt*24.0
U = SITE.g()*max(0.0, depth - gw)*A; FSu = W_empty/U if U else float('inf')
qa_d = min(3*qa, qa*(1 + 0.2*(depth/0.3048 - 1)))                    # IBC 1806.3.1 depth increase, max 3 x table
q_gross = W_srv/A; q_over = gs*depth; q_net = q_gross - q_over
sw = WT.seismic_wind(r, P.PLATE_L, P.PLATE_W); M = sw['M_seis_kNm'] + sw['V_seis_kN']*depth
e = M/W_srv; B = Wp; q_max = W_srv/A*(1 + 6*e/B) if e <= B/6 else 2*W_srv/(3*Lp*(B/2 - e))
q_max_net = q_max - q_over
ok = lambda b: 'pass' if b else 'FAIL'
md = ['# Foundation design', '', 'Document number: AQS-BLD-017', 'Revision: B', 'Date: 2026-10-25',
      'Authority: AQS-PLAN-007 task X-BLD-03; assumption A-M-208. Generated by `docs-authority/_foundation.py`; do not edit this page by hand. Study; this page is not stamped by a Professional Engineer (PE).', '',
      '| Rev | Description | Date |', '|---|---|---|', '| A | First issue | 2026-10-16 |',
      '| B | Purpose and scope added; text rewritten to the documentation style guide (AQS-DOC-002). No load, dimension or result changed. | 2026-10-25 |', '',
      '## 1. Purpose and scope', '',
      'The foundation carries the weight of the building, its equipment and its stored water into the ground, and keeps the building from '
      'overturning in an earthquake or floating when the groundwater is high. This page sizes the foundation and records the checks of bearing '
      'pressure, overturning, uplift and punching shear.', '',
      '## 2. Basis', '',
      f'The foundation is a single concrete mat (raft) under the whole {Lp:.0f} x {Wp:.0f} m plate, at {depth:.1f} m below grade, which is the floor level of CATCH_TANK (AQS-BLD-014). The soil properties are those assumed in AQS-SITE-002: an expansive clay with a presumptive allowable bearing pressure of {qa:.0f} kPa (IBC 1806.2) and a unit weight of {gs:.0f} kN/m3. The bearing pressure is an assumption until a geotechnical investigation is made to IBC 1803. The groundwater is taken at {gw:.1f} m, the worst case.', '',
      '## 3. Checks', '',
      'Table 3.1 gives each check. D, F and L are the dead load, the load of contained water and the live load; M is the overturning moment and e its eccentricity on the mat of width B; FS is the factor of safety; phiVc is the design punching-shear strength of the raft, and t its thickness.', '',
      'Table 3.1. Foundation checks', '',
 '| Check | Demand | Capacity | Result |', '|---|---|---|---|',
 f'| Service weight D + F + L | {W_srv:,.0f} kN (equipment and water {OP:,.0f}, slabs {nlev*slab*A:,.0f}, raft {raft_kN:,.0f}, walls {walls_kN:,.0f}, columns {frame_kN:,.0f}) | - | - |',
 f'| Gross bearing | {q_gross:.0f} kPa | - | - |',
 f'| Net bearing (gross - {q_over:.0f} kPa excavated overburden) | {q_net:.0f} kPa | {qa_d:.0f} kPa ({qa:.0f} x depth increase, IBC 1806.3.1) | {ok(q_net <= qa_d)} |',
 f'| Seismic overturning, M = {M:,.0f} kNm, e = {e:.2f} m (B/6 = {B/6:.2f}) | net toe {q_max_net:.0f} kPa | {qa_d:.0f} kPa | {ok(q_max_net <= qa_d)} |',
 f'| Uplift, plant empty and reservoirs drained, groundwater at {gw:.1f} m | {U:,.0f} kN | {W_empty:,.0f} kN, FS {FSu:.2f} (need 1.10) | {ok(FSu >= 1.10)} |',
 f'| Raft two-way shear at the interior column (Pu {Pu_int:.0f} kN, column {b_col*1000:.0f} mm) | {Pu_int:.0f} kN | phiVc {phiVc:.0f} kN at t = {t_shear:.2f} m | pass |',
 f'| Raft thickness adopted | shear {t_shear:.2f} m + uplift ballast {dt:.2f} m | {t_raft:.2f} m | - |', '',
 '## 4. Discussion', '',
 'The basement is a compensated foundation: the soil removed for it weighs about as much as the building, so the net bearing pressure on the clay is low. ' + (f'Uplift governs the thickness of the raft. With groundwater at grade, the empty structure would be lifted by the water, so the raft is thickened by {dt:.2f} m to act as ballast. A permanently drained basement, with an underdrain to the CATCH_TANK sump, or tension piles would remove the need for this ballast; the choice waits on a measurement of the groundwater level.' if dt > 0 else ''),
 '', 'Expansive clay swells and shrinks with its moisture content (IBC 1808.6). At this depth the raft bears below the active zone in which that movement occurs, and the slab-on-grade around the building is separated from the structure.']
open('docs-authority/FOUNDATION.md', 'w').write('\n'.join(md) + '\n'); print(round(q_gross), round(q_net), round(q_max_net), round(FSu, 2), t_raft, depth)
